 Here's where I think a lot of the problem was:

  All potions are weight 20, all spellbooks (besides the book of the dead) are weight 50:

  50 a blessed spellbook of finger of death
  50 a blessed spellbook of force bolt
  50 a blessed spellbook of magic missile
 380 19 potions of holy water
  40  2 uncursed potions of acid
  40  2 blessed potions of acid
  40  2 uncursed potions of levitation
  20 an uncursed potion of full healing
  80  4 uncursed potions of speed
---------------------------------------
 750 total weight.

  The weight of the spellbooks could have been avoided by 
slightly better preparation.

 4 potions of holy water, the potion of full healing made 
sense.  So that's about 650 unnecessary weight, or about
an extra 140 weight out of the bag.

 The rest of the holy water could have been used to bless
objects in inventory => have the effect without the weight.

 Levitation could have been blessed and quaffed when appropriate
on the plains of Air/Water.

  Ditto for speed.  (Or used for alchemy).

  The question then becomes, if dumping the extra potions/ 
spellbooks had made you unburdened before the gold/amulets/
golf bag of artifacts, etc., would you have burdened yourself
anyway?

  Another point is that you could have had nine more wishes
easily.  Why not wish for dilithium crystals?

